# E216 — Boost.Build invalid Linux target on OHOS
id:                     E216
trigger_tool:           b2|clang++
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        --target=arm64-pc-linux.*cstddef.*file not found|b2.*no-op.*target|failed clang-linux.compile.c++
severity:               2
category:               ohos, boost-build, toolchain
match_keywords:         b2, Boost.Build, arm64-pc-linux, cstddef, clang++, target triple, OHOS
title:                  Boost.Build injects an invalid Linux target triple on OHOS
root_cause:             Boost.Build can invoke the OHOS clang wrapper with --target=arm64-pc-linux. That triple bypasses the SDK's native OHOS C++ header discovery, causing cstddef lookup failures; some cached targets may instead no-op. Removing only this injected target preserves the SDK default triple.
affected_scope:         Boost.Build test targets using the OHOS clang wrapper, verified on Boost.Test 1.84.0.
verification_cmd:       b2 -d+2 <target>; rerun emitted clang++ command without --target=arm64-pc-linux
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           compiler-wrapper
rec_description:        Use a narrow compiler wrapper or direct invocation that removes only --target=arm64-pc-linux; retain all other b2 flags, then compile, link and run each affected target.
rec_command:            clang++ <b2 flags with --target=arm64-pc-linux removed>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               compiler-wrapper
forbid_1_pattern:       remove.*all.*target|replace.*with.*generic.*linux
forbid_1_reason:        Removing unrelated flags or forcing another Linux target can hide ABI and sysroot errors.
principles:             P013, P014, P020
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E074]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               doc/E216.md
last_updated:           2026-10-11
source_event:           Boost.Test 1.84.0 OHOS device validation
authors:
source_pr:
source_commit:
metrics_success_count:  4
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.9
metrics_last_used:      2026-10-11
